CherryTree 1.7.2: license, source and configuration

The unmodified Debian 13 amd64 release package is obtained from:
https://github.com/giuspen/cherrytree/releases/download/v1.7.2/cherrytree_1.7.2-2.Debian13_amd64.deb
SOURCE.json records its SHA-256 digest. solve.sh unpacks the package with
dpkg-deb; package maintainer scripts are not run and product files are not patched.

CherryTree is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. LICENSE contains the complete
GNU GPL version 3. LICENSES/cherrytree.txt preserves the package copyright and
component notices. The original notices also remain in the extracted package.
The corresponding source for version 1.7.2 is available at:
https://github.com/giuspen/cherrytree/releases/download/v1.7.2/cherrytree_1.7.2.tar.xz
Its digest is recorded in SOURCE.json.

The local start.sh, launch.py and solve.sh adapt the runtime configuration:
English labels, state under DATA_DIR, no timed autosave, no start dialog or
online version check, and an inert embedded-terminal shell. launch.py applies
Landlock before starting the product, restricting readable resources, executable
programs and writable instance/exchange directories. It refuses to start if
Landlock cannot be established. These launchers are separate from upstream code.

